[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute this into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m First, let's simplify the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=508551)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 4i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)
